# Vanilla: Expanded TODO List:
    ## Issues:
        ☑ UI: give recipe book a set of category tabs for easier navigation between different types of recipes.
        ☐ Design a better separation of alloy calculator inventory ownership/liveness validation, transfer permissions, and storage-versus-machine access policy. Reconsider the storage-class whitelist without weakening ownership or withdrawal checks, and define coverage for vanilla and modded containers.
        
    ## Recipe Book:
        ☑ Recipe book follows the inventory in "Fixed" mode and allows independent repositioning in "Movable" mode.
        ☑ recipes list box has no background or border styling, making it visually blend with the rest of the dialog.
        ☑ "Handbook" button has no left/right padding for its text.
        ☐ Redesign recipe-menu tabs to look more like nice tabs and less like plain buttons.
        ☑ "hide uncraftable" controls needs a tooltip to describe the functionality.
        ☑ "sort by" controls needs a tooltip to describe the functionality.
        ☑ recipe menus titlebar should have a little "options" button for additional settings and controls. the first setting should be the option for "remember recipe menu open state".
        ☑ Design the "Show recipes using this/these items" functionality. which should function by the player placing items into their grid and then the recipe book increses the sorting priority of relevant recipes.
        ☑ Add a craftable-only toggle that shows recipes whose ingredients are currently available, independently combining with category and search filters.
        ☐ Add favorites: let players star recipe outputs and browse a Favorites tab, with favorites saved between game sessions.
        ☑ Add a compact ingredient have/need summary beneath the tooltip's recipe preview, highlighting missing amounts in red without restoring verbose diagnostic text.
        ☑ Remember the recipe book's selected category, search text, and scroll position when closing and reopening the inventory.
        ☑ Add a shortcut to open the selected output's native handbook page.
        ☐ Add a Recent section for recipes whose ingredients were recently placed through the menu; track ingredient placement, not assumed completion of crafting.
        ☑ Add an Availability/Name sort selector, retaining current availability ordering as an option and providing stable alphabetical browsing.
        ☑ Improve empty-state feedback to distinguish no search matches from no craftable recipes in the selected category, with a quick action to clear the relevant filter.
        ☑ Add "clear" button (as a typical 'x' within a filled circle) to inner right side of search box.
        ☑ Create icons for each of the recipe categories to improve visual navigation within the recipe book.

    ## New Features:
        ☐ Add HUD indicator to show current arrow type and quantity when player is holding a bow.
        ☐ Add HUD indicator for current approximate time of day (becomes less accurate the longer the player is away from the sun).
        ☐ Add HUD indicator for current weather conditions (e.g., rain, snow, fog).
        ☐ Add HUD indicator for outside temperature when approaching a level outside the players comfort zone.
        ☐ Add HUD indicator for player body temperature when approaching dangerous levels.
        ☐ Temporal gear amulets should provide information about when the next storm is expected to occur (approximately, with increasing accuracy as the storm gets closer).
        ☐ Wearing a temporal gear amulet should provide a subtle HUD indicator when a storm is approaching.
        ☐ Targeted items such as tools on toolracks have a subtle highlight to indicate that they are targeted.

    ## Death Penalties:
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *bag* items on death (items in inventory are lost, items on hotbar and equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *unequipped* items on death (items in inventory and hotbar are lost, equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *all* items on death (items in inventory, hotbar, equipped armor & weapons are lost).
        ☐ Tool degradation on death: all tools in inventory and hotbar lose <configurable percent> durability on death.

    ## Effects:
        ☐ Blocks with light level 1 have subtle haze/smoke particles (to indicate the edge of lit areas) (reuse the existing temporal storm ground particle effect).

# Vanilla: Rebalanced Ideas:
    Note: this is a different mod from Vanilla: Expanded, I'm just keeping the ideas list here for now.
    ## Recipes:
        ☐ Candles from animal fat (render fat into tallow -> tallow replaces wax in candle recipe).

    ## Monster Rebalancing:
        ☐ Monsters cant spawn under roofs.
        ☐ Increase gear drop rates from monsters (and trading costs for gears) by 500%. this will make fighting monsters feel more rewarding.
        ☐ Add other items to monster drops (bones, scrapmetal, metal parts (uncommon), gems (rare), etc) to make them more rewarding to fight.
